Q: Indent with tabs instead of spaces in XML A: <p>The accepted answer (which is not really an answer, it is a question, and as such it should have been a comment,) does absolutely nothing to solve the problem presented by the question. I have no idea why it was posted as an answer, why it was upvoted, and why it was accepted. (Maybe it worked 10 years ago?)</p>
<p>What <em><strong>does</strong></em> solve the problem is the following:</p>
<pre><code>using( System.IO.TextWriter textWriter = ... )
{
    using( System.Xml.XmlTextWriter xmlTextWriter = new( textWriter ) )
    {
        xmlTextWriter.Formatting = System.Xml.Formatting.Indented;
        xmlTextWriter.IndentChar = '\t';
        xmlTextWriter.Indentation = 1;
        xmlDocument.WriteTo( xmlTextWriter );
    }
}
</code></pre>
